const stepTextPara = stepHeaderPara;
const stepConclusionPara = `m-0 text-[#62584b] text-[0.92rem] leading-[1.56] pt-[8px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] max-[760px]:text-[0.84rem] max-[420px]:text-[0.72rem]`;
const mathDisplayBase = `grid gap-0 min-w-0 pt-[18px] justify-items-center content-start justify-center min-h-0 text-center max-[760px]:pt-[14px] max-[760px]:min-h-0`;
---

<section id="research" class="paper-section">
  <div class="container paper-shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <span class="section-kicker">Research</span>
      <h2>Formalizing federated PKI as a governed weighted graph.</h2>
      <p>
        The proposal introduces a formal layer above PKIX semantics, representing
        certification authorities and governed federation relationships as a directed,
        weighted graph that can be queried for valid and optimal certification paths
        across classical, hybrid, and post-quantum domains.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="research-grid grid grid-cols-2 gap-[24px] mt-[42px] max-[1080px]:grid-cols-1">
      <article class="research-card p-[28px_26px] bg-gradient-to-b from-[var(--paper-card)] to-[var(--paper-card-strong)] border border-[var(--paper-border)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[var(--shadow-paper)] max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
        <div class="research-card-header flex items-baseline gap-[14px] mb-[18px] max-[760px]:items-start max-[760px]:gap-[16px]">
          <h3 class="m-0 [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] font-normal text-[2rem] leading-none max-[760px]:text-[2.25rem] max-[760px]:leading-[0.98]">Governed trust graph</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-soft)] leading-[1.8]">
          Instead of inheriting trust from entire hierarchies, PolarisChain models
          trust as explicit graph edges between governed certification authorities,
          each carrying both a technical cost and hard governance constraints.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-[18px] mb-0 pl-[18px] text-[var(--ink-soft)] [&_li+li]:mt-[10px]">
          <li>Vertices represent individual CAs within independent EJBCA instances — one instance per administrative domain.</li>
          <li>Edges encode admissible inter-domain cross-certificates; internal hierarchical relations within the same domain are not federation edges.</li>
          <li>The model preserves PKIX validation while making federation semantics explicit, computable, and queryable.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="research-card p-[28px_26px] bg-gradient-to-b from-[var(--paper-card)] to-[var(--paper-card-strong)] border border-[var(--paper-border)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[var(--shadow-paper)] max-[760px]:p-[22px]">
        <div class="research-card-header flex items-baseline gap-[14px] mb-[18px] max-[760px]:items-start max-[760px]:gap-[16px]">
          <h3 class="m-0 [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] font-normal text-[2rem] leading-none max-[760px]:text-[2.25rem] max-[760px]:leading-[0.98]">Optimal path semantics</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[var(--ink-soft)] leading-[1.8]">
          The proposal defines a normalised multicriteria cost over federation edges
          so path selection becomes a deterministic optimisation problem rather than
          an exhaustive heuristic search.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-[18px] mb-0 pl-[18px] text-[var(--ink-soft)] [&_li+li]:mt-[10px]">
          <li>Edge weights capture cryptographic posture, algorithm family, key strength, and structural distance — each normalised to [0, 1].</li>
          <li>Dijkstra-based traversal operates exclusively over governance-admissible paths, not the full graph.</li>
          <li>The result is an explainable, policy-compliant certification chain comparable against BFS as a non-weighted baseline.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="model-section mt-[30px] max-[760px]:mt-[24px]" aria-labelledby="mathematical-model-heading">
      <div class="model-heading max-w-[860px]">
        <span class="note-label">Mathematical model</span>
        <h3 id="mathematical-model-heading" class="mt-[12px] mb-0 text-[#1e1b17] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(2rem,3vw,2.8rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">A compact formalization of governed federation and path cost.</h3>
        <p class="mt-[12px] mb-0 text-[var(--ink-soft)] leading-[1.72]">
          PKIX certificate validation remains intact. The graph layer makes admissible
          trust propagation explicit, separates normalised technical edge cost from hard
          governance constraints, and selects routes only among policy-compliant
          federation paths. Edge attributes are derived automatically from X.509
          extensions of real cross-certificates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="model-grid block mt-[18px]">
        <article class="research-card model-story-card p-[clamp(22px,2.2vw,30px)] bg-gradient-to-b from-[rgba(241,233,220,0.9)] to-[rgba(232,222,206,0.96)] border border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] shadow-[var(--shadow-paper)] overflow-hidden max-[760px]:p-[16px]">
          <div class="model-story-flow grid gap-0">

            <!-- 01 Formal definition -->
            <section class="model-step grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px]" aria-labelledby="model-formal-definition">
              <div class="model-step-header model-step-header-cost grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">01</span>
                <h4 id="model-formal-definition" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Formal definition</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>
                  The federated PKI ecosystem is modeled as a four-component governed weighted graph:
                </p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase}`} aria-label="G equals open parenthesis V comma E comma w comma Phi close parenthesis">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">G</span> = (<span class="math-var italic">V</span>, <span class="math-var italic">E</span>, <span class="math-var italic">w</span>, &Phi;)</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p class={`${stepHeaderPara} mt-[4px] text-[0.82rem] italic`}>
                  Domain distinction: an administrative domain groups CAs under a shared governance policy. In the lab, each EJBCA instance (Docker container) represents one domain. Edges E only exist between CAs of distinct containers.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <p class="model-step-label m-0 text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.78)] text-[0.82rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]">where:</p>
                <dl class="model-definition-list m-0 grid gap-0 border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.09)]">
                  {formalDefinitions.map((item) => (
                    <div class="model-definition-item grid grid-cols-[minmax(160px,0.34fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-y-[6px] gap-x-[10px] py-[8px] border-b border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.09)] last:border-b-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[3px] max-[760px]:py-[6px]">
                      <dt class="m-0 grid gap-[3px] content-start">
                        <span class={`model-definition-term text-[#3a2f24] [font-family:'STIX_Two_Text','Cambria_Math','STIX_Two_Math','Times_New_Roman',serif] leading-[1.28] tracking-[0.01em] [text-rendering:optimizeLegibility] text-[clamp(0.88rem,0.88vw,0.96rem)]`} set:html={item.termHtml}></span>
                      </dt>
                      <dd class="m-0 text-[#62584b] text-[0.8rem] leading-[1.44] max-[760px]:text-[0.76rem] max-[420px]:text-[0.72rem]">{item.description}</dd>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 02 Cost function -->
            <section class="model-step model-step-cost grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] pb-[28px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px] max-[760px]:pb-[20px]" aria-labelledby="model-cost-function">
              <div class="model-step-header grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">02</span>
                <h4 id="model-cost-function" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Cost function</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>
                  Technical and structural cost is expressed as a normalised weighted sum,
                  explicitly separated from governance constraints:
                </p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase} pb-[10px] max-[760px]:pb-[10px]`} aria-label="w of e equals alpha times c crypto plus beta times c alg plus gamma times c key plus delta times c dist">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">w</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>) = &alpha; &middot; <span class="math-var italic">c</span><sub class={subClasses}>crypto</sub>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>+ &beta; &middot; <span class="math-var italic">c</span><sub class={subClasses}>alg</sub>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>+ &gamma; &middot; <span class="math-var italic">c</span><sub class={subClasses}>key</sub>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>+ &delta; &middot; <span class="math-var italic">c</span><sub class={subClasses}>dist</sub>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)</span>
                  </p>
                  <p class={`math-line ${mathLineBase} text-[clamp(0.82rem,0.9vw,0.88rem)] mt-[6px] opacity-80`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>&alpha; + &beta; + &gamma; + &delta; = 1,</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>each component <span class="math-var italic">c</span><sub class={subClasses}>x</sub>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>) &isin; [0, 1]</span>
                  </p>
                </div>

                <!-- w(e) component cards -->
                <div class="cost-component-grid grid grid-cols-2 gap-[10px] mt-[4px] max-[420px]:grid-cols-1">
                  {costComponents.map((comp) => (
                    <div class="cost-card p-[12px_14px] bg-[rgba(255,252,248,0.7)] border border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.1)] rounded-[8px]">
                      <div class="cost-card-term text-[#3a2f24] [font-family:'STIX_Two_Text','Cambria_Math','STIX_Two_Math','Times_New_Roman',serif] text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.2]" set:html={comp.termHtml}></div>
                      <div class="cost-card-range text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.6)] text-[0.72rem] font-mono mt-[2px] mb-[6px]">{comp.range}</div>
                      <div class="cost-card-desc text-[#62584b] text-[0.78rem] leading-[1.38] mb-[6px]">{comp.description}</div>
                      <div class="cost-card-examples text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] text-[0.7rem] font-mono leading-[1.4]">{comp.examples}</div>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <p class="model-step-label m-0 text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.78)] text-[0.82rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em] flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-[8px] gap-y-[4px]">
                  <span>Algorithm scoring table</span>
                  <span class="px-[8px] py-[2px] bg-[rgba(60,120,80,0.12)] text-[rgba(40,90,55,0.9)] text-[0.68rem] font-semibold rounded-[4px] tracking-[0.02em]">derived from real X.509 extensions</span>
                </p>
                <div class="algo-table-wrap w-full -mx-[2px] min-w-0 max-[760px]:mx-0 max-[760px]:overflow-x-auto">
                  <table class="algo-score-table w-full border-collapse">
                    <colgroup>
                      <col class="col-algo" />
                      <col class="col-domain" />
                      <col class="col-score" />
                      <col class="col-score" />
                      <col class="col-score" />
                      <col class="col-cost" />
                    </colgroup>
                    <thead>
                      <tr class="border-b border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.12)]">
                        <th class="th-algo text-left py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]">Algorithm</th>
                        <th class="th-domain text-left py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]">Domain</th>
                        <th class="text-center py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]"><span class="[font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] italic">c</span><sub class="text-[0.7em]">cry</sub></th>
                        <th class="text-center py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]"><span class="[font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] italic">c</span><sub class="text-[0.7em]">alg</sub></th>
                        <th class="text-center py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]"><span class="[font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] italic">c</span><sub class="text-[0.7em]">key</sub></th>
                        <th class="text-center py-[6px] px-[10px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.7)] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]"><span class="[font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] italic">w</span>(<span class="[font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] italic">e</span>)</th>
                      </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                      {algorithmScores.map((row) => {
                        const variant = row.costClass === 'score-low-good' ? 'good' : row.costClass === 'score-medium' ? 'mid' : 'bad';
                        return (
                          <tr class="border-b border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.07)] last:border-b-0">
                            <td class="td-algo py-[7px] px-[10px] text-[#3a2f24] font-mono leading-[1.25]">{row.algorithm}</td>
                            <td class="td-domain py-[7px] px-[10px] text-[#62584b] leading-[1.25]">{row.domain}</td>
                            <td class="py-[7px] px-[10px] text-center"><span class={`score-pill score-pill-${variant} font-mono`}>{row.crypto}</span></td>
                            <td class="py-[7px] px-[10px] text-center"><span class={`score-pill score-pill-${variant} font-mono`}>{row.alg}</span></td>
                            <td class="py-[7px] px-[10px] text-center"><span class={`score-pill score-pill-${variant} font-mono`}>{row.key}</span></td>
                            <td class="py-[7px] px-[10px] text-center"><span class={`score-pill score-pill-${variant}`}>{row.cost}</span></td>
                          </tr>
                        );
                      })}
                    </tbody>
                  </table>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 03 Governance constraints per edge -->
            <section class="model-step grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px]" aria-labelledby="model-governance-per-edge">
              <div class="model-step-header grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">03</span>
                <h4 id="model-governance-per-edge" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Governance constraints<br />per edge</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>
                  For each edge <span class="math-var italic">e</span> &isin; <span class="math-var italic">E</span>, the governance layer defines the hard constraints that determine whether trust may propagate through that relation at all:
                </p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase}`} aria-label="Phi of e equals the tuple of all governance components">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>&Phi;(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>) = &langle;<span class="math-var italic">prop</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">depth</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">scope</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>),</span>
                  </p>
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display math-line-indent ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay} pl-[clamp(0px,0.55vw,6px)] max-[760px]:pl-0`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">pol</span><sup class={supClasses}>+</sup>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">pol</span><sup class={supClasses}>-</sup>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">name</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">ku</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">eku</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>),</span>
                  </p>
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display math-line-indent ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay} pl-[clamp(0px,0.55vw,6px)] max-[760px]:pl-0`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">time</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>), <span class="math-var italic">crypto_floor</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)&rangle;</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <p class="model-step-label m-0 text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.78)] text-[0.82rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]">where:</p>
                <dl class="model-definition-list model-definition-list-governance m-0 grid gap-0 border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.09)]">
                  {governanceComponents.map((item) => (
                    <div class="model-definition-item model-definition-item-governance grid grid-cols-[minmax(160px,0.34fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-y-[6px] gap-x-[10px] py-[8px] border-b border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.09)] last:border-b-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[3px] max-[760px]:py-[6px]">
                      <dt class="m-0 grid gap-[3px] content-start">
                        <span class={`model-definition-term text-[#3a2f24] [font-family:'STIX_Two_Text','Cambria_Math','STIX_Two_Math','Times_New_Roman',serif] leading-[1.28] tracking-[0.01em] [text-rendering:optimizeLegibility] text-[clamp(0.88rem,0.88vw,0.96rem)]`} set:html={item.termHtml}></span>
                        {item.relationHtml && (
                          <span class={`model-definition-relation text-[rgba(76,63,48,0.84)] [font-family:'STIX_Two_Text','Cambria_Math','STIX_Two_Math','Times_New_Roman',serif] leading-[1.28] tracking-[0.01em] [text-rendering:optimizeLegibility] text-[clamp(0.82rem,0.82vw,0.9rem)]`} set:html={item.relationHtml}></span>
                        )}
                        {item.x509 && (
                          <span class="x509-source text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.55)] text-[0.68rem] font-mono leading-[1.3]">X.509: {item.x509}</span>
                        )}
                        {item.isNew && (
                          <span class="new-badge inline-block px-[6px] py-[1px] bg-[rgba(60,120,80,0.12)] text-[rgba(40,90,55,0.9)] text-[0.65rem] font-semibold rounded-[3px] tracking-[0.02em] w-fit">new</span>
                        )}
                      </dt>
                      <dd class="m-0 text-[#62584b] text-[0.8rem] leading-[1.44] max-[760px]:text-[0.76rem] max-[420px]:text-[0.72rem]" set:html={item.description}></dd>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                </dl>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 04 Admissible paths -->
            <section class="model-step grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px]" aria-labelledby="model-admissible-paths">
              <div class="model-step-header grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">04</span>
                <h4 id="model-admissible-paths" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Admissible paths</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>For a candidate path:</p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase}`} aria-label="P equals e 1, e 2, ellipsis, e k">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">P</span> = (</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">e</span><sub class={subClasses}>1</sub>,</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">e</span><sub class={subClasses}>2</sub>,</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>&hellip;,</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">e</span><sub class={subClasses}>k</sub>)</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
                <p class={`model-step-text ${stepTextPara}`}>the set of admissible paths is defined as:</p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase}`} aria-label="P adm equals set of P in script P such that P satisfies Phi">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">P</span><sub class={subClasses}>adm</sub> = &#123;</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">P</span> &isin; 𝒫</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>|</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">P</span> &#8872; &Phi;</span>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>&#125;</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <p class={`model-step-text ${stepTextPara}`}>
                  Here, <span class="math-var italic">P</span> &#8872; &Phi; means that the path satisfies all governance constraints simultaneously.
                </p>
                <ol class="model-condition-list m-0 pl-[1.05rem] text-[#62584b] text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.5] grid gap-[3px] max-[760px]:text-[0.76rem] max-[420px]:text-[0.72rem]">
                  {admissibleConditions.map((item) => (
                    <li>{item}</li>
                  ))}
                </ol>
                <div class="phi-composition mt-[8px] p-[14px_16px] bg-[rgba(255,252,248,0.6)] border border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.1)] rounded-[8px]">
                  <p class="m-0 mb-[8px] text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.78)] text-[0.78rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.02em]">Φ composition along a path:</p>
                  <dl class="m-0 grid gap-0">
                    {pathCompositionRules.map((r) => (
                      <div class="grid grid-cols-[80px_1fr] gap-x-[10px] py-[4px] border-b border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.07)] last:border-b-0">
                        <dt class="m-0 text-[#3a2f24] [font-family:'STIX_Two_Text',serif] text-[0.8rem] leading-[1.4]">{r.label}</dt>
                        <dd class="m-0 text-[#62584b] text-[0.76rem] leading-[1.4] font-mono">{r.rule}</dd>
                      </div>
                    ))}
                  </dl>
                </div>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 05 Optimal path -->
            <section class="model-step grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px]" aria-labelledby="model-optimal-path">
              <div class="model-step-header grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">05</span>
                <h4 id="model-optimal-path" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Optimal path</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>
                  The optimal route is computed only over admissible paths. Governance,
                  scope, policy, and propagation constraints are enforced before
                  optimisation begins:
                </p>
                <div class={`model-math-display ${mathDisplayBase}`} aria-label="P star equals arg min over P in P adm of sum over e in P of w of e">
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay}`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}><span class="math-var italic">P</span><sup class={supClasses}>*</sup> = arg min<sub class={subClasses}><span class="math-var italic">P</span> &isin; <span class="math-var italic">P</span><sub class={subClasses}>adm</sub></sub></span>
                  </p>
                  <p class={`math-line math-line-display math-line-indent ${mathLineBase} ${mathLineDisplay} pl-[clamp(0px,0.55vw,6px)] max-[760px]:pl-0`}>
                    <span class={`math-piece ${mathPiece}`}>&Sigma;<sub class={subClasses}><span class="math-var italic">e</span> &isin; <span class="math-var italic">P</span></sub> <span class="math-var italic">w</span>(<span class="math-var italic">e</span>)</span>
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <p class={`model-step-text ${stepTextPara}`}>
                  Non-admissible relations do not compete as merely expensive alternatives — they are excluded from the search space altogether. Route optimisation therefore occurs only after governance, scope, policy, propagation, and cryptographic floor constraints have already been enforced.
                </p>
                <p class={`model-step-conclusion ${stepConclusionPara}`}>
                  PKIX validation semantics remain unchanged. The graph layer does not replace certificate validation; it governs admissible trust propagation and computes the minimum-cost route only across policy-compliant federation paths. BFS over the full graph 𝒫 serves as the non-weighted evaluation baseline.
                </p>
              </div>
            </section>

            <!-- 06 Laboratory correspondence -->
            <section class="model-step grid grid-cols-[minmax(440px,0.62fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-[28px] py-[14px] border-t border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.08)] first:pt-0 first:border-t-0 last:pb-0 max-[760px]:grid-cols-[1fr] max-[760px]:gap-[10px] max-[760px]:py-[12px]" aria-labelledby="model-lab-correspondence">
              <div class="model-step-header grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pr-[10px] max-[760px]:pr-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <span class="model-step-marker inline-block text-[rgba(95,81,62,0.66)] text-[0.74rem] font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">06</span>
                <h4 id="model-lab-correspondence" class="m-0 text-[#1f1a15] [font-family:'Playfair_Display',serif] text-[clamp(1.7rem,2.4vw,2.15rem)] font-normal leading-[0.98] max-[760px]:text-[1.28rem] max-[760px]:leading-[1.04]">Model–laboratory correspondence</h4>
                <p class={stepHeaderPara}>
                  Each component of the formal model has a concrete realisation in the
                  EJBCA CE infrastructure deployed over Docker containers on Proxmox.
                  Three homogeneous domains provide cryptographic diversity at the
                  federation layer without intra-domain heterogeneity.
                </p>
              </div>
              <div class="model-step-body grid content-start gap-[14px] min-w-0 pt-[62px] max-[760px]:pt-0 max-[760px]:gap-[9px]">
                <div class="domain-grid grid grid-cols-1 gap-[10px]">
                  {domains.map((d) => (
                    <div class={`domain-card p-[12px_16px] border border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.1)] rounded-[8px] domain-card-${d.colorClass}`}>
                      <div class="domain-name text-[#3a2f24] text-[0.88rem] font-semibold leading-[1.2] mb-[4px]">{d.name}</div>
                      <div class="domain-algo text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.8)] text-[0.75rem] font-mono mb-[4px]">{d.algo}</div>
                      <div class="domain-detail text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.6)] text-[0.72rem]">{d.detail}</div>
                    </div>
                  ))}
                  <div class="domain-card p-[12px_16px] border border-[rgba(70,60,45,0.1)] rounded-[8px] bg-[rgba(255,252,248,0.5)]">
                    <div class="domain-name text-[#3a2f24] text-[0.88rem] font-semibold leading-[1.2] mb-[4px]">Bridges — Federation nodes</div>
                    <div class="domain-algo text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.8)] text-[0.75rem] font-mono mb-[4px]">BridgeCA-AB (composite) · BridgeCA-BC (ML-DSA-65) · BridgeCA-AC (ML-DSA-65) · BridgeCA-Gov (RSA-4096)</div>
                    <div class="domain-detail text-[rgba(88,75,58,0.6)] text-[0.72rem]">1 EJBCA instance · 4 Bridge CAs · individual crypto_floor per bridge policy</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class={`${stepConclusionPara} mt-[4px]`}>
                  Edge attributes w(e) and Φ(e) are derived automatically from the X.509 extensions of each cross-certificate via BouncyCastle .NET 2.5.0 (native ML-DSA support). The SQL Graph is populated without manual intervention. Federation topology is declared in <code class="font-mono text-[0.8em] bg-[rgba(70,60,45,0.07)] px-[4px] py-[1px] rounded-[3px]">federation-topology.yaml</code> and cross-certificates are issued through the EJBCA REST API.
                </p>
              </div>
            </section>

          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="research-notes mt-[30px] pt-[26px] border-t border-[rgba(52,46,39,0.12)] grid grid-cols-3 gap-[24px] max-[1080px]:grid-cols-1">
      <div>
        <span class="note-label">Research problem</span>
        <p>
          Certification path discovery becomes increasingly difficult as multidomain PKI federations grow denser and cryptographically heterogeneous.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="note-label">Methodological lens</span>
        <p>
          Directed weighted graphs, normalised multicriteria cost, deterministic shortest-path computation, and policy-aware trust modelling over real X.509 infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div id="interoperability">
        <span class="note-label">Interoperability objective</span>
        <p>
          Support controlled interoperability across classical, hybrid, and post-quantum PKI domains without requiring a shared trust root or modifying PKIX validation semantics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

